From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wlanapi: interfaces, scan, networks and interface queries through sg-netctl (3541)

wlanapi: interfaces, scan, networks and interface queries through sg-netctl

WlanEnumInterfaces lists the wireless adapters NetworkManager has (via sg-netctl), WlanScan starts a rescan and calls the registered notification when it is done (WlanRegisterNotification keeps the callback), WlanGetAvailableNetworkList returns the scan result (SSID, signal quality, security, connected/has-profile flags), WlanQueryInterface answers interface_state, autoconf_enabled, background_scan_enabled, media_streaming_mode, bss_type and hosted_network_capable. Reading only: connecting, profiles and the hosted network are not done.

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto earlier integration patches: clean 3-way merge.
